diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..abeb127
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Quizzy
+
+A local-first Rails app for preparing and playing live conference quizzes.
+
+Create or import a quiz in the moderator area, then choose **Start a game**. Share the on-screen link or QR code with players. Use **Start**, **Finish**, **Next**, and **End quiz** to run the talk; phones and the big screen update automatically. Every new game has independent players and answers.
+
+In quiz **Settings**, set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** for an automatic per-question limit. Both default to 0 (no timer). Only the moderator sees the countdown; reloads preserve it, and **Finish** still closes a question early. Timer settings are local and are not exported.
+
+## Run
+
+Dependencies are installed and pinned in `Gemfile.lock`. Set these environment variables:
+
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE`
+- `QUIZZY_MODERATOR_USERNAME`
+- `QUIZZY_MODERATOR_PASSWORD`
+- `PORT` (optional; defaults to `3000`)
+
+Then run `bin/serve`. It prepares SQLite, compiles assets, and starts production Puma in the foreground. Visit `/moderate` and sign in with HTTP Basic authentication. `/up` is the readiness endpoint.
+
+All quiz data lives under `storage/`. Assets and fonts are local; the app requires no external services.
+
+## Test
+
+Run `bin/rails test`. See [implementation notes](docs/implementation.md) for the production Chromium smoke test and architectural details.
